3. Datasets used in the experiments
-----------------------------------

Belebele (facebook/belebele, revision 7899cdfa4e1e0d733fd77c848e2c273cb1d32be2), configs swe_Latn and
eng_Latn. Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Credit:
Bandarkar et al. (2024), "The Belebele Benchmark: a Parallel Reading Comprehension Dataset in 122
Language Variants", ACL 2024. This repository holds only question ids and our models' results
(results/experiments/analysis/other_exams/), not the Belebele texts. The data is downloaded at the
pinned revision by analysis/other_exams.py.

MMLU (cais/mmlu, revision c30699e8356da336a370243923dbaf21066bb9fe), three mathematics subjects.
Licence: MIT, "Copyright (c) 2020 Dan Hendrycks". Credit: Hendrycks et al. (2021), "Measuring
Massive Multitask Language Understanding", ICLR 2021. This repository holds only question ids and
our models' results, not the MMLU texts.

Riksdagen open data (data.riksdagen.se), speeches of the 2025/26 session, in data/damage/ and
repeated as prompts in the generations.jsonl files of the run folders.
  Källa: Sveriges riksdag
  Source: The Swedish Parliament
The Riksdag is not behind this project and has not endorsed it. The speeches contain personal data
(speakers' names and statements). Terms: https://www.riksdagen.se/sv/dokument-och-lagar/riksdagens-oppna-data/anvandarstod/anvandningsvillkor/
Details are in data/damage/SOURCES.md.

Högskoleprovet (UHR, studera.nu). Only question ids, answer letters, model answers and checksums
are published. Two short example items are quoted in the report under the quotation right
(22 § upphovsrättslagen), with UHR named as the source. Everything else is rebuilt locally with
`make data` (see report/DATA_RIGHTS.md and REPRODUCE.md).
